#: server.py:33
msgid "home page title"
msgstr "LM Toolbox — Home"

#: server.py:38
msgid "privacy page title"
msgstr "LM Toolbox — Privacy policy"

#: server.py:43
msgid "news page title"
msgstr "LM Toolbox — News"

#: templates/home.html:18
msgid "closed testing eyebrow"
msgstr "Open source · closed testing on Google Play"

#: templates/home.html:20
msgid "lm toolbox tagline"
msgstr "One app, a drawer full of tools for Android: measuring, electronics, media, a Minecraft server and more. Open source, and sold on Google Play, where it is currently in closed testing: ask me to add your Gmail address as a tester to get access."

#: templates/home.html:22
msgid "Join testing"
msgstr "Join testing"

#: templates/home.html:23
msgid "View on GitHub"
msgstr "View on GitHub"

#: templates/home.html:24
msgid "Contact via email"
msgstr "Contact via email"

#: templates/home.html
msgid "features title"
msgstr "What's inside"

#: templates/home.html
msgid "features lead"
msgstr "Tools you would otherwise need a dozen apps for, in English and Polish, with no ads, accounts or tracking."

#: templates/home.html
msgid "feature measure title"
msgstr "Measure"

#: templates/home.html
msgid "feature measure"
msgstr "Ruler, spirit level and compass (both with home screen widgets), sound level meter, light meter, metal detector, vibration meter and a stroboscope / tachometer."

#: templates/home.html
msgid "feature electronics title"
msgstr "Electronics"

#: templates/home.html
msgid "feature electronics"
msgstr "30 calculators: resistor color and SMD codes, Ohm's law, RC, RL and RLC filters, voltage divider, transistor, op-amp, LED resistor, 555 timer, LM317, PCB trace width, number bases and more."

#: templates/home.html
msgid "feature reference title"
msgstr "Reference"

#: templates/home.html
msgid "feature reference"
msgstr "29 references: pinouts drawn on screen (Raspberry Pi GPIO, Arduino, USB, HDMI, ATX, OBD-II…) and tables such as E-series, wire gauges, ASCII, thermocouples and car fuses."

#: templates/home.html
msgid "feature media title"
msgstr "Media"

#: templates/home.html
msgid "feature media"
msgstr "Download, convert and shrink videos, music and images; edit a photo's metadata; make QR codes; check file hashes (MD5, SHA-1, SHA-2, SHA-3, CRC32)."

#: templates/home.html
msgid "feature finance title"
msgstr "Finance"

#: templates/home.html
msgid "feature finance"
msgstr "A currency converter with the European Central Bank's daily rates; share an amount to it from any app."

#: templates/home.html
msgid "feature servers title"
msgstr "Servers"

#: templates/home.html
msgid "feature servers"
msgstr "Run your own Minecraft server (Vanilla, Paper, Fabric, Forge or NeoForge) straight from your phone, reachable by your friends through Bore, a Cloudflare tunnel or Tailscale."

#: templates/home.html
msgid "features linux"
msgstr "The heavier tools run real Linux programs (Python, FFmpeg, yt-dlp, ExifTool, Java) in a built-in subsystem that the app installs piece by piece, only when a tool needs it. No root, no terminal."

#: templates/home.html
msgid "open source title"
msgstr "Open source"

#: templates/home.html
msgid "open source"
msgstr "The app's code is public under the GNU GPL v3: read it, learn from it, or build the app yourself."

#: templates/home.html
msgid "open source play"
msgstr "Buying it on Google Play is the easy way to get it, with automatic updates, and it's what supports its development. Thank you!"

#: templates/home.html
msgid "open source brand"
msgstr "The license covers the code, not the brand: the app's name, icon and Google Play listing aren't under the GPL, so a published fork needs its own name, icon and application ID."

#: templates/home.html
msgid "Source code"
msgstr "Source code"

#: templates/home.html
msgid "Linux subsystem"
msgstr "Linux subsystem"

#: templates/news.html:10
msgid "news title"
msgstr "News"

#: templates/news.html:11
msgid "news note"
msgstr ""
"This feed powers the in-app news updates — there's nothing to see here "
"directly."

#: templates/privacy.html:10
msgid "privacy policy title"
msgstr "Privacy policy"

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy intro"
msgstr "This policy describes how the LM Toolbox app (org.lukemech.lmtoolbox), developed by Łukasz Błaszczyk, handles your data, and when it connects to the internet."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy data title"
msgstr "Data collected by the developer"

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy data"
msgstr "None. The app has no account, no analytics, no advertising, no crash reporting and no tracking of any kind. Nothing you do in the app or create with it is sent to the developer, sold, or shared with third parties."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy network title"
msgstr "Internet access"

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy network"
msgstr "The app uses the internet only for the features listed below. Each connection goes straight from your device to the named service which, like any server, sees your IP address and basic request details (such as the app's or tool's identifier)."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy network news"
msgstr "News feed: on the home screen, at most once every two hours, the app downloads short news about the app (and their images) from toolbox.lukemech.org. The request includes only your device's language, to pick the right translation."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy network rates"
msgstr "Currency Converter: downloads the daily reference exchange rates published by the European Central Bank (ecb.europa.eu). Nothing about you or your conversions is sent."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy network downloader"
msgstr "Media Downloader: when you give it a link, the app (using the open-source yt-dlp tool) connects to the website of that link to fetch the media you asked for, and saves it on your device. Those websites' own terms and privacy policies apply; the developer never sees your links or downloads. You are responsible for downloading only content you have the right to download."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy network play"
msgstr "Tools installed on demand: some tools are delivered as Google Play modules, downloaded by Google Play when you install them, under Google's privacy policy."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy network links"
msgstr "Links you open (e.g. from the news feed, the settings or a QR code) open in your browser or another app of your choice."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy network security"
msgstr "All of the app's own connections use encrypted HTTPS."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy device title"
msgstr "Permissions and data on your device"

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy device location"
msgstr "Location: used only by the compass and its widget, if you allow it, to show the altitude from GPS (the widget keeps reading it while it's on your home screen). It is processed on the device and never sent anywhere."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy device files"
msgstr "Files: photos, videos and other files you open, edit, convert, hash or download are processed locally on your device (by the bundled ExifTool, FFmpeg and Python among others) and stay there."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy device notifications"
msgstr "Notifications: used only to show background work, such as downloads and conversions, a running Minecraft server and live widgets."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy device backup"
msgstr "Settings: stored on your device. If you have Android backup turned on, they may be included in your device's backup to your Google account, under Google's terms."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy server title"
msgstr "This website"

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy server"
msgstr "toolbox.lukemech.org uses no cookies, analytics or trackers. Like any web server, it may briefly keep technical logs (IP address, time and requested address) for its operation and security; they are not used to identify anyone and are not shared."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy use title"
msgstr "Use of the app"

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy use"
msgstr "The app is sold through Google Play: purchases, payments and refunds are handled by Google under Google Play's terms, and the developer never receives your payment details. To the extent permitted by law, the app is provided \"as is\", without warranty; it is currently in testing and may contain bugs. This does not limit your statutory consumer rights. Use its tools lawfully and with respect for others' rights, including copyright and the terms of the websites you download from. The app's own code is licensed under the GNU GPL v3, and the bundled open source components are under their own licenses, listed in the app's settings."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy deletion title"
msgstr "Deleting your data"

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy deletion"
msgstr "Since all data stays on your device, you can delete it at any time by clearing the app's data or uninstalling it. Files you saved to your device's storage stay until you delete them."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy children title"
msgstr "Children"

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy children"
msgstr "The app is not directed at children and knowingly collects no data from anyone, including children."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy changes title"
msgstr "Changes to this policy"

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy changes"
msgstr "If the app changes how it handles data, this page will be updated before or together with that version, and the date below will change."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy contact title"
msgstr "Contact"

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy contact"
msgstr "Questions about this policy or the app:"

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy open source"
msgstr "The app is open source, so everything below can be checked in its code:"

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy network minecraft"
msgstr "Minecraft server: to create or update a server, the app gets the version lists and server files straight from their publishers (Mojang, PaperMC, FabricMC, Minecraft Forge, NeoForged). Players connect to your server directly, or through a tunnel you turn on; the server and its worlds stay on your device."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy network tunnels"
msgstr "Server tunnels, only if you turn one on: Bore connects to bore.pub (or a Bore server you choose), and a Cloudflare tunnel connects to Cloudflare with the token you entered; checking a domain for it asks Cloudflare's DNS (cloudflare-dns.com). Those services' terms and privacy policies apply. Tailscale is a separate app, which the server's page only opens."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy device microphone"
msgstr "Microphone: used only by the sound level meter, if you allow it, and only while its page is open, to measure loudness. Sound is never recorded, saved or sent anywhere."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy device sensors"
msgstr "Sensors, torch and vibration: the measuring tools read the device's sensors (the vibration meter at a high sampling rate), the stroboscope flashes the torch, and the metal detector can vibrate. None of it leaves the device."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy device awake"
msgstr "Keeping the device awake: while a Minecraft server runs, the app keeps the phone and its Wi-Fi from sleeping, so players stay connected."

#: templates/privacy.html
msgid "privacy device share"
msgstr "\"Share to\" and \"Open with\": some tools appear in Android's share menu; each entry can be turned off in the tool's settings, and the app sees only what you share with it."

#: templates/privacy.html:13
msgid "last updated"
msgstr "Last updated"

